SysUISdk — composed Android SDK platform for the SystemUI-Gradle project
=========================================================================

This archive contains the ``android-SysUISdk`` compile platform used by the
SystemUI-Gradle project (https://github.com/convivae/SystemUI-Gradle).

WHAT THIS IS
------------
A drop-in Android SDK *platform* directory that lets a standard Gradle/AGP
build compile AOSP SystemUI sources which reference ``@hide`` APIs,
aconfig-generated flags classes, and framework-private resources that the
stock Android SDK platform does not expose.

It is a compile-time platform only. Nothing from it is packaged into the
built APK.

PROVENANCE AND LICENSE STACK
----------------------------
This platform is machine-composed by ``tools/build_sysuisdk.py`` (Apache
License 2.0, part of the SystemUI-Gradle project) from two sources:

1. AOSP-derived components — Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE):

   * Framework class bytecode merged into ``android.jar`` (built from the
     AOSP ``framework`` module, release tag ``android-17.0.0_r1``).
   * The complete framework resource set in ``android.jar``
     (``resources.arsc`` + ``res/**``), byte-exact from the AOSP-built
     ``framework-res.apk``.
   * Hidden AIDL declarations appended to ``framework.aidl``, derived from
     AOSP primary sources.
   * Bridge class entries in ``android.jar`` and
     ``core-for-system-modules.jar``, byte-exact from AOSP-built
     ``core-libart``, ``aconfig-annotations`` and ``keepanno-annotations``
     jars.

2. Stock Android SDK Platform components (base platform ``android-37.0``,
   published by Google):

   * Files copied verbatim from the stock platform package, including but
     not limited to ``data/``, ``skins/``, ``templates/``, ``optional/``,
     ``android-stubs-src.jar``, ``uiautomator.jar``, ``build.prop``,
     ``sdk.properties``, and the stub-only entries of ``android.jar`` /
     ``core-for-system-modules.jar`` that were not overlaid by AOSP bytes.

   These components remain governed by the Android SDK License Agreement
   (https://developer.android.com/studio/terms). By using them you agree to
   those terms. They are redistributed here unmodified, solely as the base
   layer of this composed platform, to enable building AOSP SystemUI outside
   the AOSP tree.

The exact per-file inventory and SHA-256 of both the base platform and the
AOSP inputs used for this build are recorded in
``android-SysUISdk/.sysuisdk-generated.json`` inside this archive.

If you prefer a base that is 100 % AOSP-sourced (Apache 2.0 throughout),
you can regenerate the platform yourself from an AOSP checkout; see the
project README ("regenerating from scratch").
